This licence covers patch_micro.py and the documentation in this folder, and
nothing else.

It does NOT cover the bitbox micro firmware. That is 1010music's work, it is not
included here in any form, and no permission over it is granted or implied — not
to the stock image you supply, and not to the patched image the script produces
from it.

Running this project's modified firmware can affect your warranty. Assume that
it does, and check 1010music's own warranty terms yourself rather than trusting
this file on the subject.

Flash the stock firmware back before sending a unit in for service. If a fault
could plausibly be connected to running modified firmware, say so when asked.
Restoring stock to tidy up an unrelated issue is reasonable; using it to hide a
relevant detail is not, and it is how goodwill for projects like this gets
destroyed for everyone.

